Z||000003||theogre||08-20-2000||12:31 PM||||Unless there is a problem with the existing coil you'll get NO benifit at all from replacing it. Now if your doing it simply as a PM thing..... Then it doesn't matter much. MSD Accell and ACDelco OE coils will all do about the same on a stock motor. Your biggest ignition reliability items are the plugs cap rotor and wires, not the coil.<P>The thing I think would help V6 and older 4 cyls more is moving the coil to a cooler location in the engine compartment. The cruise control mount would be a good spot for cars w/o that option. (I wish I could move the DIS brick. I have to develope a good extension method for the crank pickup to do that.)<P>There is no "Best" coil. Just like there's no "Best" allot of things for a car. It all depends on your exact application and driving paterns. In my headlight article soon to be posted I review what I consider a Best headlight for allot of applications but that doesn't make it Best for everyone.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||RobertVol||08-20-2000||12:43 PM||||DIS CAP AND ROTOR HAVE been replaced. but ever since I had my Tach filter going out my car has been having what I would call a miss on highway speeds and a little bit it of a jerk in acceleration and it seems to be when the tach jumps. I was going to replace that with a part from Rodneys but wanted to check and see if thats whats causing the problem. but I have never had this problem... were the heck is it? And since I was replacing thought I might as well replace the coil while fooling around with it. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||08-20-2000||12:49 PM||||On my 3.4 I went with an MSD Blaster 2 coil. It is the oil filled canister type instead of the GM hei style that it replaced. I did this for a few reasons- <BR>Oil filled coils usually stay cooler.<BR>Higher voltage output. <BR>I already had it, so it only made sense to use it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I did follow Ogre's advice and mounted it on the rear firewall where the cruise master used to be. <P>------------------<BR>The slower they think you are, the more suprised they will be when you smoke them.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DXR_DAD||08-20-2000||12:51 PM||||Robert, Ogre said it a little better than I did, but that's why hes Theogre!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>The ignition is all one system. I replaced it all, New distributor, cap, plugs, Accel 300+ wires, coil.<P>MSD blaster replacement coil GM #121-8226 $38.99 from JEG"S<P>Accel 300+ universal fit $60.00. I wanted to make them up myself so I could do the routing to keep them all off and away from heat exhaust.<P><BR>DXR_DAD ||||reg||14
Z||000007||theogre||08-20-2000||01:25 PM||||unplug the tach filter and see if the problem goes away..... That will tell you really quick. The tach filter can and will screw up the coil firing. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||olympic||08-20-2000||01:39 PM||||  I'd have to vote for the Jacobs Electronics ignition system.  It comes with a <B>HUGE</B> ignition coil, a computer control unit and super low resistance spiral core wires.  I've had their mileage master kit for over a year with excellent results.  The idle is smoother and part throttle acceleration and high rpm torque were also better.  Its probably a result from widening the spark gap  nearly 100%.  Mine is set around 0.070" with good results. <P>  The only drawback is that you have to run regular plugs.  ie-no platinum or V-groove or split fire, etc.  Jacobs claims that the computer uses each plug as an "in cylinder" sensor and platinum and other plugs will screw up the readings.  Jacobs also has many other kits for racing or pro street.||||reg||1
Z||000009||RobertVol||08-20-2000||03:24 PM||||MAN ! <P>I unplugged the filter and it made a HUGE HUGE difference! things runs like brand new. <BR>Is this one of those things we can do without? other than the tach working? <P>if needed I guess I will get one from Rodney ||||reg||1
Z||000010||theogre||08-20-2000||04:14 PM||||Yes you can run w/o it. the only thing affected will be no tach.||||reg||1
